<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anthonie Heinsius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1641">1641</a>–<a href="/years/1720">1720</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anthonie Heinsius was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-pensionary">Grand Pensionary</a> of Holland from 1689 until his death in 1720 and a close ally of the stadtholder and English king William III. After William's death in 1702 he directed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> policy in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>, working with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-churchill-1st-duke-of-marlborough">Duke of Marlborough</a> and Prince Eugene against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. The war's cost left the Republic heavily indebted, and the Peace of Utrecht of 1713 brought it few gains.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anthonie-heinsius.jpg" alt="Anthonie Heinsius" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gerbrand van den Eeckhout · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1659_portrait_of_a_man,_Possibly_of_Anthonie_Heinsius.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
